    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, our offensive engine is centered around **James Wood** (78.42) and **Mickey Moniak** (75.75), who emerge as our premier starts due to ideal matchup profiles. **James Wood** benefits significantly from a favorable park factor and, crucially, a slow opposing delivery that invites stolen base opportunities, a priority given our league\u2019s scarcity. Similarly, **Mickey Moniak** is locked in as a high-floor play, leveraging a strong dynamic platoon advantage and an aggressive #2 lineup spot against Bradley. **Corbin Carroll** (75.42) also remains a core asset, despite a slight deduction for the opposing pitcher's pickoff efficiency, his raw speed and matchup versus Martinez keep him in the elite tier of our daily distribution.\n\nWe are navigating a few tactical hurdles, specifically the 35% rain risk for **Jose Caballero** (67.15) and several \"Lineup Pending\" designations for **Austin Riley**, **Max Muncy**, **Henry Bolte**, and **Tyler Soderstrom**. While **Tyler Soderstrom** boasts a strong 71.48 score, his utility is predicated on that #4 slot assignment. The most difficult bench decision involved **Travis Bazzana** (51.16). While his #1 order spot offered upside, he simply couldn't clear the efficiency threshold set by our active starters. **Seiya Suzuki** was also considered, but the combination of a tough matchup against a sub-3.00 xERA pitcher and our reliance on efficiency metrics relegated him to the bench. We are proceeding with this configuration to maximize our 5x5 categories, closely monitoring the weather in **Jose Caballero**'s game to determine if a late-swap is required to protect our game cap usage.",
